#
# Counter-example for the native math:ExactPreservationViolated gate (FactorGraph arm): a
# math:FactorGraph declares logic:preservationKind logic:ExactPreservation DIRECTLY on
# itself but declares no math:dependencyGraph, so its completeness gate (finite factors,
# normalized or declared unnormalized) cannot hold — the honest-when-complete exactness
# claim made explicit for a model that cannot honor it. The native gate MUST emit
# math:ExactPreservationViolated (and no other probability failure class); in particular
# math:IncompleteDependencyModel MUST stay silent — an instance that is structurally
# incomplete AND itself declares logic:ExactPreservation is Gate 5's overclaim, not Gate
# 4's plain structural-incompleteness report, so the two gates never co-fire on the same
# instance.
# Back-reference: math:FactorGraph / math:ExactPreservationViolated
# (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:overclaimedFactorGraph a math:FactorGraph ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:ExactPreservation .
